## ⚙️ 5. (Optional) Add dependencies or libraries

If your binary needs shared libraries (like `libssl.so`), you can use `autoPatchelfHook` to fix runtime paths automatically:

```nix
{ stdenv, autoPatchelfHook, openssl, zlib }:

stdenv.mkDerivation {
  pname = "mybinary";
  version = "1.0";

  src = ./mybinary;
  dontUnpack = true;

  nativeBuildInputs = [ autoPatchelfHook ];
  buildInputs = [ openssl zlib ];

  installPhase = ''
    mkdir -p $out/bin
    cp $src $out/bin/mybinary
    chmod +x $out/bin/mybinary
  '';
}
```

This automatically patches the ELF binary to find the right dynamic libraries in the Nix store.

